  "scope_note": "DORA covers 5 pillars: ICT risk management (Art. 5-15), incident reporting (Art. 17-23), digital operational resilience testing (Art. 24-27), third-party risk (Art. 28-44), and information sharing (Art. 45). The bulk of DORA is process and contractual — much of it cannot be verified externally. This file maps only the articles whose technical requirements have an externally-observable signal: Art. 7 (ICT systems/protocols/tools), Art. 8 (asset identification), Art. 9 (protection/prevention/encryption), Art. 10 (detection), Art. 28 (third-party JS supply chain). Articles 5-6 (governance), 11-16 (response/recovery/learning), 17-23 (incident reporting), 24-27 (testing programs), 29-44 (contractual third-party risk) are intentionally absent — auditors verify those from documentation, not external scans. Mandatory for EU financial entities (banks, insurance, investment firms, payment institutions, crypto-asset service providers) since 17 January 2026.",
